{
  "summary": "The change makes the MessagePack analyzer keep validating [MessagePackObject(SuppressSourceGeneration = true)] types while skipping source generation for them. The three F1 contract-diagnostic tests pass and the F2 test (source-generation-only diagnostics not reported) passes, but the analyzer still crashes with AD0001 on duplicate string keys in a suppressed type, so the full suite fails one new test and N1 is not met; tests.fail_without_fix was not run, so N2 cannot be determined.",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "All three F1 tests pass on head: MemberWithoutKeyIsReported (MsgPack004), MemberTypeMustBeMessagePackObjectIsReported (MsgPack003), and AllowPrivateRequiredIsReported (MsgPack015); the duplicate-key diagnostic MsgPack005 is also reported (the duplicate-string test fails only on the extra analyzer-crash diagnostic, tracked under N1).",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberWithoutKeyIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberTypeMustBeMessagePackObjectIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.AllowPrivateRequiredIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateIntKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MixedKeyKindsAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "passed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-F2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed passes on head, and the code skips the AOT init-property check when suppressed (line 989) and returns before the partial-type check when SuppressSourceGeneration is true (lines 1383-1386).",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 989, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (suppressSourceGeneration is not true && isInitOnly)"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1383, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (suppressSourceGeneration is true)"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1386, "rev": "head", "quote": "return null;"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-N1",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "The full suite fails because DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure produces a second diagnostic AD0001 (analyzer crash) in addition to the expected MsgPack005, so the analyzer still crashes on duplicate string keys in a suppressed type.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1039, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (true)"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1041, "rev": "head", "quote": "stringMembers.Add(member.StringKey, (member, item.Type));"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-N2",
      "verdict": "cannot_determine",
      "confidence_basis": "The tests.fail_without_fix check was not run for this revision, so it cannot be established that the new tests fail without the fix and pass with it; additionally DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure fails on head, so pass-with-fix does not hold for every new test.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "failed"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "N1",
      "title": "Analyzer crashes (AD0001) on duplicate string keys in a suppressed type",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "GetObjectInfo reports MsgPack005 for the duplicate key but then executes `if (true) { stringMembers.Add(...) }` for properties, which throws ArgumentException on the already-existing key and crashes the analyzer, producing an extra AD0001 diagnostic. The intMembers and field-stringMembers branches guard with ContainsKey, but the property stringMembers branch does not.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.DuplicateStringKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1039, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (true)"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1041, "rev": "head", "quote": "stringMembers.Add(member.StringKey, (member, item.Type));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1023, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(member.IntKey))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1179, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (!stringMembers.ContainsKey(member.StringKey))"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Change line 1039 from `if (true)` to `if (!stringMembers.ContainsKey(member.StringKey))` so the property branch matches the intMembers and field branches and does not re-add an already-reported duplicate key."
    },
    {
      "id": "N2",
      "title": "Inconsistent duplicate-key guard and dead `if (true)` block",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "claim": "The property branch wraps stringMembers.Add in `if (true)` (always true), while the equivalent intMembers and field-stringMembers branches use `if (!ContainsKey(...))`. The `if (true)` block is dead-looking code and is the direct cause of finding N1.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1039, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (true)"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1023, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(member.IntKey))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1179, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (!stringMembers.ContainsKey(member.StringKey))"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Replace `if (true)` with `if (!stringMembers.ContainsKey(member.StringKey))` for consistency with the other two branches."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "Performance impact of the added ContainsKey checks in TypeCollector",
      "reason": "No performance check was run for this revision; the cost of the extra dictionary lookups is not measured.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner / performance reviewer",
      "blocking": false
    },
    {
      "topic": "Public API and analyzer-rule impact",
      "reason": "The public_api and analyzers checks were not run for this revision, so any impact on the public API or analyzer rules is undecided.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
